      ":question/problem": "The rate at which guests check into a particular hotel one evening is given by the function\n\n$$\nr(t)=3{t}^{2}+2,\n$$\n\nwhere $r(t)$ is measured in guests per hour and $t>0$ is the time in hours since $\\text{6}\\,\\text{p.m}.$\n\nGuests are also checking out of the hotel at a steady rate of $1$ guest per hour.\n\nIf there were $200$ guests in the hotel at $6\\,\\text{p.m},$ how many guests will there be in the hotel at $9\\,\\text{p.m?}$"
