      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-62822",
      ":question/problem": "Larry's laptop is infected with a virus. The rate at which the files are infected is given by the function\n\n$r(t) = t^{2} + 8t + 8$,\n\nwhere $r(t)$ is measured in files per hour and $t > 0$ is the time in hours since the virus started to spread.\n\nLarry's laptop has a weak antivirus that starts working immediately. The antivirus software heals infected files at a rate of $2t + 8$ files every hour.\n\nIf the laptop had $30$ infected files initially, how many files are infected after $6$ hours?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
