      ":question/problem": "Engineers are testing a water pump filling a reservoir.\nThey observe that water enters the reservoir at a rate $r(t)$ given by the function\n\n$$\nr(t)=12\\sqrt{t+4},\n$$\n\nwhere $r(t)$ is measured in gallons per minute, and $t>0$ is the time in minutes since the pump was turned on.\nAt the same time, water leaks from the reservoir at a constant rate of $6$ gallons per minute.\n\nIf the reservoir was initially empty, find the expression that gives $V(t),$ the volume of water in the reservoir $t$ minutes after the pump was turned on.\n\n$V(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,6t-64$"
