      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-62825",
      ":question/problem": "A tank has an inlet and an outlet. When the inlet is turned on, the rate at which water flows into the tank governed by the function\n\n$$\nr(t)=9{t}^{2}+18,\n$$\n\nwhere $r(t)$ is measured in liters per minute and $t>0$ is the time in minutes.\n\nWhen the outlet is switched on, water leaves the tank through it at a rate of $14$ liters per minute.\n\nThe inlet is switched on, and the water level increases to $120$ liters, at which point the outlet is also switched on. How much water is in the tank $10$ minutes after switching on the outlet, given that the outlet is switched on at $t=0?$"
    }
